WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:02.868
Maisie!
It is so good to see you.

00:00:02.868 --> 00:00:04.137
-Hi!
-You look fantastic.

00:00:04.137 --> 00:00:05.804
-Thank you for having me back.

00:00:05.804 --> 00:00:07.506
-So happy to have you b--

00:00:07.506 --> 00:00:09.308
Wait. We have to talk about
the last time you were on

00:00:09.308 --> 00:00:12.545
because seriously --
-It was crazy.

00:00:12.545 --> 00:00:16.949
-It was April Fool's,
and we pranked our audience

00:00:16.949 --> 00:00:19.618
to think that you spoiled
"Game of Thrones," the ending.

00:00:19.618 --> 00:00:21.154
-The end of the show.

00:00:21.154 --> 00:00:24.823
Not just your audience.
The entire world.

00:00:24.823 --> 00:00:28.428
-I think it's over
24 million hits on YouTube.

00:00:28.428 --> 00:00:30.030
-It's crazy.

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:32.532
That was probably
the most successful thing

00:00:32.532 --> 00:00:34.700
I did last year,
and I was on the final season

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:37.369
of "Game of Thrones."

00:00:37.369 --> 00:00:38.938
-No, I mean -- Well, gosh.

00:00:38.938 --> 00:00:41.908
In case you haven't seen it,
here's our April Fool's prank.

00:00:41.908 --> 00:00:43.843
Take a look at this.
This is a prank.

00:00:43.843 --> 00:00:47.346 line:0%
-When I found that Arya died
in, like, the second episode,

00:00:47.346 --> 00:00:50.516 line:0%
I was...

00:00:50.516 --> 00:00:53.619 line:0%
-Are you s-- What?
-Is this live?

00:00:53.619 --> 00:00:56.122 line:0%
-No.
-We can edit that.

00:00:56.122 --> 00:00:57.723 line:0%
-Are you serious?
-Yeah.

00:00:57.723 --> 00:00:59.291 line:0%
-Let's talk about
the final season.

00:00:59.291 --> 00:01:02.161 line:0%
-I'm s--

00:01:02.161 --> 00:01:03.863 line:0%
-Is she okay?

00:01:03.863 --> 00:01:06.199 line:0%
I'm gonna just go...

00:01:08.467 --> 00:01:11.237 line:0%
-April Fool's!

00:01:11.237 --> 00:01:13.639
-Dude, honestly.
I have to stop there.

00:01:13.639 --> 00:01:15.074
I could never top that.

00:01:15.074 --> 00:01:17.276
That's the best acting
I've ever done in my life.

00:01:17.276 --> 00:01:19.579
We work well together.

00:01:19.579 --> 00:01:22.414
But you --
you started shaking and, like...

00:01:22.414 --> 00:01:24.484
And I was like...
-You know,

00:01:24.484 --> 00:01:27.887
I find these
talk shows in person

00:01:27.887 --> 00:01:29.789
actually more nerve-racking

00:01:29.789 --> 00:01:30.923
than it is, like,
sitting in my kitchen.

00:01:30.923 --> 00:01:33.392
But I was so nervous
coming on the show,

00:01:33.392 --> 00:01:35.595
and I'm such a big fan
of the show,

00:01:35.595 --> 00:01:37.263
and I'd never done it before.

00:01:37.263 --> 00:01:41.100
And so I basically
was just letting myself --

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:44.403
letting all of the nerves
just come out in that moment.

00:01:44.403 --> 00:01:47.406
And I can hear people
in the audience,

00:01:47.406 --> 00:01:49.609
and they're whispering,
and I'm thinking,

00:01:49.609 --> 00:01:51.177
"Oh, they're not buying it."

00:01:51.177 --> 00:01:52.578
And, like, when I look back now,

00:01:52.578 --> 00:01:55.314
I realize that it was probably,
like, nervous laughter.

00:01:55.314 --> 00:01:58.017
But at the time, I was like,
"They are not buying this.

00:01:58.017 --> 00:02:01.587
I'm going to have to ham this up
and, like, turn on the tears

00:02:01.587 --> 00:02:03.222
and get these people...
-No, you did.

00:02:03.222 --> 00:02:04.757
You had the tears.
They were just --

00:02:04.757 --> 00:02:07.693
They were on the edge.
Like a meniscus around your eye.

00:02:07.693 --> 00:02:10.163
And I was like --
And then I felt so bad.

00:02:10.163 --> 00:02:11.831
This is like so --

00:02:11.831 --> 00:02:14.133
I do not do tricks.
I don't do pranks.

00:02:14.133 --> 00:02:16.068
I go, "Oh, no, no, no."
I felt so bad for you

00:02:16.068 --> 00:02:17.569
'cause it was
your first time on,

00:02:17.569 --> 00:02:18.838
and I'm making you do this bit.

00:02:18.838 --> 00:02:21.473
And I go --
And then -- Oh, my gosh.

00:02:21.473 --> 00:02:23.509
Honestly, I was exhausted.

00:02:23.509 --> 00:02:26.845
I can't even imagine
what you go through acting,

00:02:26.845 --> 00:02:29.148
because if that's
what acting is,

00:02:29.148 --> 00:02:30.516
I'm not cut out for that at all.

00:02:30.516 --> 00:02:32.184
I was exhausted.

00:02:32.184 --> 00:02:34.620
I had to take like a month off

00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:37.089
just to sleep
and get my energy back.

00:02:37.089 --> 00:02:39.926
-You nailed it.
It was just beautiful.

00:02:39.926 --> 00:02:42.561
Any time you're in a movie,

00:02:42.561 --> 00:02:44.564
I've got to be in that movie
with you.

00:02:44.564 --> 00:02:47.400
-We have good chemistry, bud.
I appreciate that.

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:50.836
You started "Game of Thrones"
when you were 12.

00:02:50.836 --> 00:02:53.406
So this is the first time
in ten years

00:02:53.406 --> 00:02:55.175
that you don't have to
worry about spoilers.

00:02:55.175 --> 00:02:58.077
How does that feel?
-It is so nice.

00:02:58.077 --> 00:02:59.712
I used to walk down the street,

00:02:59.712 --> 00:03:03.483
and every single person
that would recognize me,

00:03:03.483 --> 00:03:05.885
the only thing they'd ever
want to know is, like,

00:03:05.885 --> 00:03:07.887
"Tell me what happens
in the next season.

00:03:07.887 --> 00:03:09.956
Did Jon Snow really die?

00:03:09.956 --> 00:03:11.924
Are you going to be
blind forever?"

00:03:11.924 --> 00:03:14.760
Like, all of these things
that I just couldn't talk about.

00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:17.897
Now I guess people
actually just ask me like,

00:03:17.897 --> 00:03:20.432
"What did you think
of the final season?"

00:03:20.432 --> 00:03:23.002
Because there's a lot
of speculation over, you know,

00:03:23.002 --> 00:03:24.336
the success of it.

00:03:24.336 --> 00:03:26.672
-Yes. Should Arya
have won the throne?

00:03:26.672 --> 00:03:28.707
Was that the right way to go?

00:03:28.707 --> 00:03:32.478
Let me tell you something. No
one wants anything good to end.

00:03:32.478 --> 00:03:34.814
There is no --
You just don't want it to end.

00:03:34.814 --> 00:03:37.483
So no matter what it was,
it's perfect.

00:03:37.483 --> 00:03:39.418
It was great.

00:03:39.418 --> 00:03:40.653
-Oh, thank you.

00:03:40.653 --> 00:03:43.356
No. We had such a blast.
We loved it.

00:03:43.356 --> 00:03:45.324
I was so happy with my ending,

00:03:45.324 --> 00:03:48.961
and it was just a beautiful end
to a decade of my life.

00:03:48.961 --> 00:03:51.964
And I just -- I couldn't be
happier with it, honestly.

00:03:51.964 --> 00:03:54.033
-When did you know?
Did you film different endings?

00:03:54.033 --> 00:03:56.168
Or did you know kind of
before it was happening?

00:03:56.168 --> 00:03:57.970
Like, oops.
-No, yeah, we --

00:03:57.970 --> 00:04:01.941
So, we just had one script
the whole time.

00:04:01.941 --> 00:04:05.010
But in terms of, like,
finding out the story,

00:04:05.010 --> 00:04:06.912
I was actually --

00:04:06.912 --> 00:04:09.315
I was at, like,
a costume fitting

00:04:09.315 --> 00:04:12.018
before we had received the
scripts for the final season,

00:04:12.018 --> 00:04:16.288
and, um, I was, like,
looking on the wall,

00:04:16.288 --> 00:04:18.791
because they had the breakdown
of every scene.

00:04:18.791 --> 00:04:20.927
Had, like, one sentence
of what was going on.

00:04:20.927 --> 00:04:22.595
And I was looking
at episode three

00:04:22.595 --> 00:04:24.497
because it was called
"The Long Night,"

00:04:24.497 --> 00:04:26.332
and I was like, "Ooh,
that sounds like a battle."

00:04:26.332 --> 00:04:29.001
And so I'm, like,
looking through,

00:04:29.001 --> 00:04:32.771
and it says,
"Arya is with B

00:04:32.771 --> 00:04:36.542
and then Arya is with the hound
and then with Mel."

00:04:36.542 --> 00:04:38.510
And all these, like,
kind of code names.

00:04:38.510 --> 00:04:43.149
And then I got to a scene,
and it said, "Arya kills NK."

00:04:43.149 --> 00:04:45.684
And I was like, "Who is NK?"

00:04:45.684 --> 00:04:50.489
Like, who -- I had no idea
which character that is.

00:04:50.489 --> 00:04:52.691
And it turns out
it was the Night King.

00:04:52.691 --> 00:04:54.459
It was like THE character.
-THE NK.

00:04:54.459 --> 00:04:57.963
-The guy to kill. NK.

00:04:57.963 --> 00:05:01.434
And I was thrilled.
Absolutely thrilled.

00:05:01.434 --> 00:05:02.634
-That was awesome.

00:05:02.634 --> 00:05:04.470
And what a performance,
too, man.

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:06.372
I was just -- It was a crusher.

00:05:06.372 --> 00:05:08.941
Congrats on all that stuff.
I want to get to your movies.

00:05:08.941 --> 00:05:11.177
But also quickly,
I saw that you've been getting

00:05:11.177 --> 00:05:13.479
into video games
the past few months,

00:05:13.479 --> 00:05:14.980
and you debated --
-I have.

00:05:14.980 --> 00:05:16.482
-Playing on Twitch.

00:05:16.482 --> 00:05:20.319
-Video games got me -- Yeah.
Got me through this lockdown.

00:05:20.319 --> 00:05:22.522
-What are you playing?
What are you playing?

00:05:22.522 --> 00:05:24.290
-I've been playing
"Animal Crossing."

00:05:24.290 --> 00:05:26.058
-Yes.

00:05:26.058 --> 00:05:27.493
-Uh, "Minecraft."

00:05:27.493 --> 00:05:30.762
I played this really great game
called "Conduct TOGETHER!"

00:05:30.762 --> 00:05:33.198
And you're basically,
like, a train conductor

00:05:33.198 --> 00:05:34.767
and you have to make sure

00:05:34.767 --> 00:05:36.969
that trains don't crash
into each other

00:05:36.969 --> 00:05:39.071
and all of the people get
picked up from their stations

00:05:39.071 --> 00:05:40.840
at the correct --
It's ridiculous,

00:05:40.840 --> 00:05:43.508
but, honestly...
it is so fun.

00:05:43.508 --> 00:05:45.044
-"Conduct TOGETHER!"?

00:05:45.044 --> 00:05:46.745
-"Conduct TOGETHER!"
-Wow.

00:05:46.745 --> 00:05:48.648
-You have to play it
with a partner, though.

00:05:48.648 --> 00:05:51.217
'Cause trying to do that,
like, alone with both --

00:05:51.217 --> 00:05:53.653
'Cause one controller
starts and stops,

00:05:53.653 --> 00:05:55.888
and the other controller...

00:05:55.888 --> 00:05:57.256
-Picks people up?

00:05:57.256 --> 00:05:59.858
-...changes the tracks.
-Oh, changes the track?

00:05:59.858 --> 00:06:01.293
-And so trying to do both,

00:06:01.293 --> 00:06:03.128
it's like scratching your head
and rubbing your tummy.

00:06:03.128 --> 00:06:05.398
-My wife will never do that
with me. No, no, no, no, no.

00:06:05.398 --> 00:06:06.699
So I could never play that game.

00:06:06.699 --> 00:06:08.301
Oh, you know what game
I'm playing, which is good?

00:06:08.301 --> 00:06:10.336
Have you played "Fall Guys"?

00:06:10.336 --> 00:06:11.804
-[ Gasps ] I just played this

00:06:11.804 --> 00:06:13.673
the other day
for the first time!

00:06:13.673 --> 00:06:16.309
-It's fun, right?
-Yes. So much fun.

00:06:16.309 --> 00:06:18.677
-If any of you at home
don't know what it is --

00:06:18.677 --> 00:06:20.813
It's probably
on all the systems.

00:06:20.813 --> 00:06:22.849
But you basically
drop out of the sky,

00:06:22.849 --> 00:06:24.950
and then you go online
against 60 people

00:06:24.950 --> 00:06:27.386
and you do, like,
an online obstacle course,

00:06:27.386 --> 00:06:29.221
and you're, like, these
blobby type of people,

00:06:29.221 --> 00:06:30.422
and it's really fun.

00:06:30.422 --> 00:06:31.757
And it's short.

00:06:31.757 --> 00:06:33.258
-They way they're animated,
as well.

00:06:33.258 --> 00:06:35.127
Like, they're so stupid.
[ Laughs ]

00:06:35.127 --> 00:06:37.730
They fall over
and, like, flip around.

00:06:37.730 --> 00:06:39.565
They're really funny.
I love them.

00:06:39.565 --> 00:06:42.367
-I'm going to get a friend and
then play "Conduct TOGETHER!"

00:06:42.367 --> 00:06:46.438
But in the meantime, you have
a few protects coming up.

00:06:46.438 --> 00:06:50.242
"The Owners" is in theaters
and on demand September 4th.

00:06:50.242 --> 00:06:54.013
This is like a creepy thriller

00:06:54.013 --> 00:06:56.983
with, like, twists,
and it's scary.

00:06:56.983 --> 00:07:00.052
Are you a fan of those movies?
-I am.

00:07:00.052 --> 00:07:01.821
Psychological thrillers are --

00:07:01.821 --> 00:07:04.023
and, like, horror
is my favorite genre.

00:07:04.023 --> 00:07:06.759
And I always love
watching these movies.

00:07:06.759 --> 00:07:08.895
And so it was
a real dream come true

00:07:08.895 --> 00:07:11.163
to be a part of
something like that.

00:07:11.163 --> 00:07:13.566
And, yeah, I mean, on set,

00:07:13.566 --> 00:07:15.601
like, you know, it's always

00:07:15.601 --> 00:07:17.869
just way more fun
than it looks on camera.

00:07:17.869 --> 00:07:19.805
You're, like, screaming
and covered in blood,

00:07:19.805 --> 00:07:21.808
and it's like a nightmare,
but on set,

00:07:21.808 --> 00:07:23.742
we're just in this, like,
beautiful home

00:07:23.742 --> 00:07:26.546
in Southwest London
in the middle of summer

00:07:26.546 --> 00:07:27.813
just, you know,
having a great time.

00:07:27.813 --> 00:07:30.149
-Screaming and covered in blood.

00:07:30.149 --> 00:07:32.317
-Yeah. Sometimes.
Occasionally.

00:07:32.317 --> 00:07:34.720
And then occasionally
having a lovely dinner.

00:07:34.720 --> 00:07:37.155
-It's a good story.
It's really fun.

00:07:37.155 --> 00:07:39.925
I was like, "Oh. Oh, wow.

00:07:39.925 --> 00:07:42.227
Okay.
So now we flip the script.

00:07:42.227 --> 00:07:44.096
Okay. Interesting."

00:07:44.096 --> 00:07:47.900
And then "The New Mutants"
is in theaters August 28th.

00:07:47.900 --> 00:07:51.136
People are freaking out
waiting for this to come out.

00:07:51.136 --> 00:07:54.840
You filmed this three years ago.
Is that correct?

00:07:54.840 --> 00:07:57.943
-Three years ago,
and we have had --

00:07:57.943 --> 00:08:00.612
I found out today this is
our fifth release date

00:08:00.612 --> 00:08:02.447
that we've ever had.

00:08:02.447 --> 00:08:04.550
And this is the first time
we've ever got this far.

00:08:04.550 --> 00:08:06.818
So our tickets went on sale
yesterday.

00:08:06.818 --> 00:08:09.021
And so it feels real this time!

00:08:09.021 --> 00:08:12.091
-It's official!
It's coming out!

00:08:12.091 --> 00:08:13.826
-Yes.
-It's coming out!

00:08:13.826 --> 00:08:16.895
-Yeah. But I'm so excited
for this movie to come out.

00:08:16.895 --> 00:08:20.065
I still love it as much as I did
the day that I signed on.

00:08:20.065 --> 00:08:23.436
And there's been a lot of rumors
as to why this film was delayed.

00:08:23.436 --> 00:08:26.272
But honestly, no other film

00:08:26.272 --> 00:08:29.475
was affected as much as ours was
in the merger.

00:08:29.475 --> 00:08:31.510
And there's no other reason
than that.

00:08:31.510 --> 00:08:35.514
People are going to love it.
It's a beautiful story.

00:08:35.514 --> 00:08:38.851
And I just can't wait
for people to finally see it.

00:08:38.851 --> 00:08:40.486
-Yeah. People are going crazy.

00:08:40.486 --> 00:08:42.989
At one point,
I read somewhere that --

00:08:42.989 --> 00:08:45.023
I think someone said
the director described it

00:08:45.023 --> 00:08:47.593
as Stephen King
meets John Hughes.

00:08:47.593 --> 00:08:50.963
-Yes. Exactly that.
Nail on the head.

00:08:50.963 --> 00:08:54.333
-Because you're teenagers.
Is that why?

00:08:54.333 --> 00:08:55.901
-Exactly. Yes.

00:08:55.901 --> 00:08:57.703
We are these, like,
teenage mutants.

00:08:57.703 --> 00:08:59.771
It's not look like
a typical superhero film

00:08:59.771 --> 00:09:01.507
where we've got it all
figured out

00:09:01.507 --> 00:09:03.009
and we're saving the world.

00:09:03.009 --> 00:09:04.676
We actually are all
kind of trapped

00:09:04.676 --> 00:09:06.545
in this medical facility,

00:09:06.545 --> 00:09:08.814
and we're trying to
harness our powers.

00:09:08.814 --> 00:09:11.216
We still don't understand
how to use them.

00:09:11.216 --> 00:09:14.086
We keep harming other people
and harming ourselves.

00:09:14.086 --> 00:09:17.456
And so it's down
to Dr. Cecilia Reyes,

00:09:17.456 --> 00:09:19.925
who is in charge
of looking after us

00:09:19.925 --> 00:09:24.697
and teaching us how to -- how to
control ourselves, effectively.

00:09:24.697 --> 00:09:27.566
But they're also just teenagers
who are just trying to grow up,

00:09:27.566 --> 00:09:30.202
and their bodies are changing,
and they also have superpowers.

00:09:30.202 --> 00:09:33.306
And I think it's just very
relatable for a lot of people,

00:09:33.306 --> 00:09:35.975
a lot of young people also.

00:09:35.975 --> 00:09:38.477
I think the younger generation
are the most resilient.

00:09:38.477 --> 00:09:39.878
They've been through so much

00:09:39.878 --> 00:09:41.546
in, like,
such a short space of time.

00:09:41.546 --> 00:09:43.883
And I think this movie
really plays into that.

00:09:43.883 --> 00:09:46.818
Like, really high stakes
and really immense pressure

00:09:46.818 --> 00:09:49.454
and also in the middle of it
just trying to be a teenager

00:09:49.454 --> 00:09:51.824
and fall in love and live life.

00:09:51.824 --> 00:09:53.592
-I want to show everyone a clip.

00:09:53.592 --> 00:09:55.861
Here is Maisie Williams
in "The New Mutants"

00:09:55.861 --> 00:09:58.998
in theaters August 28th.
Take a look.

00:09:58.998 --> 00:10:01.000
[ Rumbling ]

00:10:01.000 --> 00:10:03.535
♪♪

00:10:03.535 --> 00:10:05.671
-It's up to us.

00:10:05.671 --> 00:10:10.375
-No. It's hunting Dani.
-Why Dani?

00:10:10.375 --> 00:10:12.711
-Because that's what she fears.

00:10:12.711 --> 00:10:16.148
Come on. Help me.

00:10:16.148 --> 00:10:17.883
-All right. One, two, three.

00:10:17.883 --> 00:10:19.284
-[ Grunts ]

00:10:19.284 --> 00:10:24.924
♪♪

00:10:24.924 --> 00:10:27.226
-Take Dani to a safe place.

00:10:27.226 --> 00:10:29.729
And I'll take care of this bear.

00:10:29.729 --> 00:10:32.097
[ Shouting in foreign language ]

00:10:32.097 --> 00:10:34.900
[ Electricity crackles ]

00:10:34.900 --> 00:10:37.269
♪♪

00:10:37.269 --> 00:10:38.871
-What are you going to do?

00:10:38.871 --> 00:10:40.439
-I'm going to play with them.

00:10:40.439 --> 00:10:41.941
-Fantastic.

